+### 1. Unpriced dollars emitted as `$0.00` (Bug, accepted)
+
+Right, and it was the same class of error I had already fixed once for the
+*derived* case without extending it to *unpriced*. A `basis` field beside a
+numeric zero does not help a consumer summing the JSON — the sum is already
+wrong.
+
+`CostTokenTotals.reported_cost_usd` / `derived_cost_usd` / `total_cost_usd` are
+now `float | None`, `None` whenever nothing behind them was priced
+([`rollup.py`](../../../../../reference/packages/eden-storage/src/eden_storage/rollup.py)).
+`_refresh_total` keeps `None` rather than summing two `None`s into `0.0`. The
+report emits JSON `null` and the table renders `n/a`; `_fmt_usd` no longer has a
+path that prints `$0.0000` for an absent figure. Applies to **every** bucket
+(`totals`, `by_role`, `by_variant`, `by_idea`, `by_model`), not just `by_model`.
+The test that codified the zero now asserts `None`, and the empty-ledger test was
+renamed — an empty ledger means "nothing recorded", not "the run was free".
+
+Each bucket also now carries `is_floor`, so the "this total understates spend"
+signal is one field instead of something a consumer derives from two counters.
+
+### 2. Evaluator idempotency keys not injective (Bug, accepted)
+
+Confirmed against the spec, not just the code: chapter 2 §1.3 keeps `task_id` /
+`variant_id` opaque with no format mandated, so `f"{task_id}-{variant_id}"`
+genuinely collides — `("task-a", "variant-b-c")` and `("task-a-variant-b", "c")`
+render one key, and first-write-wins then discards a real attempt's spend. That
+is the one error this ledger must not make. This is the same "ids are opaque"
+trap AGENTS.md records for *parsing* ref names, hit while *composing* one.
+
+New `composite_attempt_key(*parts)` length-prefixes each part, which is
+injective by construction. The evaluator uses it; so does the **ideator**, whose
+`task_id`+nonce join had the same defect and which the review didn't name.
+
+Fixing it surfaced a second latent bug the review didn't reach: a max-length pair
+would have exceeded `CostEntry.entry_id`'s 128-char cap, raised inside
+`record_outcome_cost`'s catch-all, and dropped the row **silently**.
+`cost_entry_id` now digests any over-cap key (deterministically, so retries still
+dedupe) instead of overflowing; truncating would have reintroduced collisions.
+`ENTRY_ID_MAX_LEN` is exported — a test needing it to assert the cap is a sign the
+cap belongs in the API.
+
+Also fixed the doc/impl drift the review caught: the docstring claimed
+`<task_id>:<variant_id>` while the code used `-`.
+
+### 3. Partially priced attempts classified as fully derived (Risk, accepted)
+
+`DerivedCost.partially_priced` is set whenever some classes priced and others had
+no rate. The rollup counts those in `entries_partially_priced` (they still carry
+dollars, so they are not "unpriced"), `is_floor` covers both shortfall kinds, and
+the table's floor line now names which applies. Previously a report could say
+"all of it DERIVED" with an unrated class silently missing from the figure.
+
